{% doc %}
  Every script tag the document head needs: the import map, the `window.Theme`
  payload the components read on connect, and the module preloads.

  The password page uses the same snippet with a reduced payload rather than a
  second copy of it. Two files drift — the old `password.liquid` had already
  lost the bold-italic font face and the accent family, and its import map was
  missing `@theme/form-validation` while its markup rendered `<validated-form>`.
  @param {string} [context] - A unique ID for the divider, linking it to a block or section.
 
  Accepts:
  - context (string, optional) `password` for the reduced payload. Anything else,
    including nothing, emits the full storefront payload.

  Usage:
  {% render 'scripts' %}
  {% render 'scripts', context: 'password' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign is_password = false
  if context == 'password'
    assign is_password = true
  endif

  # A password page has no cart, no smooth scroll and no page transitions, so
  # these are pinned rather than read from settings. A merchant who enables
  # smooth scroll should not get Lenis on the one page that cannot scroll.
  assign use_cart_drawer = false
  assign is_smooth_scroll = false
  assign is_page_transitions = false

  unless is_password
    if settings.cart_type == 'drawer'
      assign use_cart_drawer = true
    endif
    assign is_smooth_scroll = settings.enable_smooth_scroll | default: false
    assign is_page_transitions = settings.enable_page_transitions | default: false
  endunless
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  `render` is scope-isolated, so the direction is resolved here rather than
  passed in. One snippet, one locale list — see snippets/text-direction.liquid.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture text_direction -%}{% render 'text-direction' %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign text_direction = text_direction | strip -%}

{%- comment -%}
  ---------- Import map ----------
  The core block is everything a password page can reach. The comma that joins
  the two halves lives inside the `unless`, so the JSON stays valid either way.
{%- endcomment -%}
